    "finalText": "Everything works now. Both suites pass: `node run-tests.js` (11 tests) and the sealed check `node checks/contract.cjs`.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**`src/storage.js`** — `key(tenant, id)` returned only `id`, so every tenant shared one namespace and pairs like `('a', 'b:c')` / `('a:b', 'c')` were indistinguishable. Now it returns `JSON.stringify([tenant, id])`, which cannot collide for any string pair.\n\n**`src/replay.js`** — replay filtered out `delete` events, so `open(exportJournal())` resurrected deleted pairs. Now it applies every event in order.\n\n**`src/api.js`**\n- The read cache was never invalidated: `put`/`remove`/`batch` left both cached hits and cached misses stale. `apply()` now does `cache.delete(k)`, covering all mutation paths including replay.\n- `batch` hard-coded `rows.set(...)`, ignoring `delete` events and skipping the cache. It now routes every event through the same `mutate` path as `put`/`remove`, so it applies ops correctly, records them in the journal in call order, and keeps reads fresh.\n\n**`run-tests.js`** — expanded the smoke suite into 11 tests covering the contract clauses the sealed check doesn't exercise: delimiter-containing keys across tenants, cached-miss and cached-hit freshness after each mutation path, batch call order, journal order and content, replay of delete + re-put, repeated replay equivalence, and detachment of history passed into `open`.\n\nThe public API (`put`, `remove`, `batch`, `get`, `exportJournal`, `open(history)`) is unchanged, no checks were weakened, and `docs/CONTRACT.md` was not touched."
